{"step_index":6103,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T11:17:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-25T11:17:11Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-25T11:17:11Z\n\nThe command exited with code 0.\nOutput:\n{\r\n  \"step_index\": 6042,\r\n  \"source\": \"MODEL\",\r\n  \"type\": \"PLANNER_RESPONSE\",\r\n  \"status\": \"DONE\",\r\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-25T11:14:41Z\",\r\n  \"thinking\": \"The `.mp4` string absence in the temporary journal is unexpected. The file system's filename storage method could be a factor. The `data.find(b'.mp4')` returning 0 needs further investigation. The database was located in a different directory than initially assumed. Awaiting clarification on where `output_packaged` resides.\\n\\n\\nThe recovered MP4s originated from `MAGIC-2`, carved from unallocated inodes on the NVMe drive `/dev/nvme1n1`. The initial count of 136 videos raises the question of where the remaining videos are located, prompting investigation of other video formats and the potentially misidentified `.unknown` files. The header bytes `ftyp` (at offset 4) will be used to identify video file headers directly within `/dev/nvme1n1`'s unallocated sectors, and thus find the other videos. A python script will be crafted to scan the raw device for these headers.\\n\\n\\n\",\r\n  \"tool_calls\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"name\": \"run_command\",\r\n      \"args\": {\r\n        \"CommandLine\": \"\\\"sudo python3 -c \\\\\\\"\\\\nimport struct, os\\\\n\\\\nprint('Scanning /dev/nvme1n1 for MP4/video ftyp headers...')\\\\nCHUNK_SIZE = 16 * 1024 * 1024 # 16 MB\\\\n\\\\nvalid_brands = [b'isom', b'iso2', b'mp41', b'mp42', b'avc1', b'qt  ', b'M4V ', b'MSNV']\\\\n\\\\ntotal_found = 0\\\\nfound_offsets = []\\\\n\\\\n# Scan first 50 GB of disk or sample\\\\nwith open('/dev/nvme1n1', 'rb') as dev:\\\\n    offset = 0\\\\n    # Let's scan up to 100 GB (or 6000 chunks of 16MB)\\\\n    for i in range(2000): # 32 GB\\\\n        chunk = dev.read(CHUNK_SIZE)\\\\n        if not chunk:\\\\n            break\\\\n        pos = 0\\\\n        while True:\\\\n            pos = chunk.find(b'ftyp', pos)\\\\n            if pos == -1:\\\\n                break\\\\n            if pos >= 4:\\\\n                brand = chunk[pos+4:pos+8]\\\\n                if brand in valid_brands:\\\\n                    # check box size\\\\n                    box_sz = struct.unpack('>I', chunk[pos-4:pos])[0]\\\\n                    if 16 <= box_sz <= 1024:\\\\n                        abs_pos = offset + pos - 4\\\\n                        found_offsets.append((abs_pos, brand))\\\\n                        total_found += 1\\\\n            pos += 4\\\\n        offset += len(chunk)\\\\n        if (i + 1) % 500 == 0:\\\\n            print(f'Scanned {(offset)/1024/1024/1024:.1f} GB... Found {total_found} MP4 headers so far')\\\\n\\\\nprint(f'Done 32 GB scan! Total MP4 headers found: {total_found}')\\\\n\\\\\\\"\\\"\",\r\n        \"Cwd\": \"\\\"/home/azureuser\\\"\",\r\n        \"WaitMsBeforeAsync\": \"8000\",\r\n        \"toolAction\": \"\\\"Scanning raw NVMe drive for all MP4 headers\\\"\",\r\n        \"toolSummary\": \"\\\"Scan raw NVMe drive for all MP4 headers\\\"\"\r\n      }\r\n    }\r\n  ]\r\n}\r\n\n"}
